# 8️⃣ Tree DP

## Problem Type

Questions on:

```text
Trees
```

where answer depends on children.

---

### State

```cpp
dp[node]
```

Meaning:

```text
Answer For Subtree
```

---

# 9️⃣ Example

Maximum subtree sum.

---

### DFS

```cpp
dfs(node,parent)
{
    for(child)
    {
        dfs(child,node);

        dp[node]
        +=
        dp[child];
    }
}
```

---

# 🔟 Tree Diameter DP

## Diameter

Longest path in tree.

---

### Idea

For every node:

Store:

```text
Largest Height

Second Largest Height
```

---

### Formula

```text
height1
+
height2
```

---

### Complexity

```text
O(N)
```

---

# 1️⃣1️⃣ DP On Trees Example

House Robber III

---

### State

```cpp
dp[node][0]

dp[node][1]
```

Meaning:

```text
Take Node

Do Not Take Node
```

---

### Recurrence

Take:

```cpp
nodeValue
+
notTake(children)
```

---

Not Take:

```cpp
max(childTake,
childNotTake)
```

---

# 1️⃣2️⃣ Rerooting DP

## Problem

Find answer for:

```text
Every Node
As Root
```

---

### Naive

```text
O(N²)
```

---

### Rerooting

```text
O(N)
```

or

```text
O(N log N)
```

---

# 1️⃣3️⃣ Idea

Compute:

```text
Answer At Root
```

Then move root.

Reuse previous computations.

---

### Common Questions

```text
Tree Distances

Subtree Sums

Tree DP
```

---

# 1️⃣4️⃣ DP Optimization

## Space Optimization

Example:

```cpp
dp[i]
depends only on

dp[i-1]
```

---

Then:

```text
Use Variables
```

instead of array.

---

### Example

Fibonacci

```text
O(N)

↓

O(1)
```

---

# 1️⃣5️⃣ State Reduction

Bad State:

```cpp
dp[i][j][k]
```

---

Try reducing.

Example:

```cpp
dp[i][j]
```

---

Improves:

```text
Memory

Runtime
```

